<!--
    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 The octagonOS Project
    SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

    The shader is compiled into the plugin rather than installed beside it.
    KWin loads it with a ":/" resource path, so there is no file to go missing
    and no path to get wrong at install time. A shader KWin cannot read is an
    effect that silently does nothing.

    No double hyphen appears in this comment: XML forbids it inside a comment
    body, and rcc rejects the whole file for it. The same mistake was made in
    the Android overlays, where aapt2 rejected them for exactly this.
-->
<RCC>
    <qresource prefix="/effects/facetui-glass">
        <file>shaders/facetui-glass.frag</file>
    </qresource>
</RCC>
